---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import sergio from '../assets/images/portrait-sergio-cartoon.png';
---
<Layout title="Sergio Aquilini | Solution Architect & .NET Developer"
        description="Sergio Aquilini: Solution Architect and senior .NET developer at Swiss Post, and author of Silverback. Experience, projects and education."
        copyright="Sergio Aquilini">
    <div id="title">
        <h1 class="terminal-title">Sergio <em>Aquilini</em></h1>
        <p class="subtitle"><span class="typing"><em>architect</em> by trade, <em>coder</em> at heart</span></p>
    </div>
    <div id="bio">
        <Image src={sergio} width={208} densities={[1, 2]} loading="eager" alt="Illustrated portrait of Sergio Aquilini"/>
        <div id="bio-details">
            <dl>
                <dt>Born</dt>
                <dd>1984</dd>
                <dt>Location</dt>
                <dd>Mesocco, Switzerland</dd>
                <dt>Languages</dt>
                <dd class="languages"><span>Italian (native)</span><span>English (C1)</span>
                    <span>German (B2)</span><span>French (A2)</span></dd>
            </dl>
            <div class="contact-links" aria-label="Contact and profiles">
                <a href="mailto:sergio@aquilini.ch">
                    <Icon name="email"/>
                    sergio@aquilini.ch</a>
                <a href="https://github.com/BEagle1984" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
                    <Icon name="github"/>
                    GitHub</a>
                <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/aquilinis/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
                    <Icon name="linkedin"/>
                    LinkedIn</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div id="resume">
        <section aria-labelledby="professional-summary">
            <h2 id="professional-summary">Professional Summary</h2>
            <p>
                I&rsquo;m a Solution Architect and senior .NET developer with over 20 years of experience.
                My work combines technical leadership with hands-on development, focusing on distributed systems
                and asynchronous messaging.
            </p>
        </section>
        <section aria-labelledby="current-role">
            <h2 id="current-role">Current Role</h2>
            <p>
                At Swiss Post, I work with fellow architects to guide development across Logistics Services,
                primarily in sorting. I work particularly closely with the sorting preparation team, whose applications
                define sorting plans and support short-term adjustments to changing operational needs.
            </p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Technical direction:</strong> guide developers on technology choices, implementation approaches
                    and API design through reviews, discussions and hands-on support.</li>
                <li><strong>Planning:</strong> work with the Product Owner to set priorities and guide development increments.</li>
                <li><strong>Integration:</strong> support other Logistics Services projects and collaborate with software
                    and hardware suppliers to integrate their solutions into our systems.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>Our team owns its services through production operation, using trunk-based development, continuous delivery
                and automated testing. We review production warnings and errors weekly, addressing issues and reducing
                log noise, and monitor application performance and resource usage to guide ongoing improvements.</p>
            <div class="technology-line">
                <strong id="stack-label">Stack</strong>
                <ul class="tags" aria-labelledby="stack-label">
                    <li>.NET</li><li>Kafka</li><li>MQTT</li><li>AWS EKS</li><li>PostgreSQL</li><li>MongoDB</li><li>Splunk</li><li>Grafana</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </section>
        <section class="feature" aria-labelledby="open-source">
            <h2 id="open-source">Open Source</h2>
            <h3>Silverback &mdash; .NET messaging library</h3>
            <p>I&rsquo;m the author and maintainer of Silverback, a library for asynchronous messaging and event-driven
                systems with Apache Kafka and MQTT integration.
                <strong>It is the standard messaging solution for all .NET applications at Swiss Post.</strong></p>
            <p>Silverback keeps me closely involved in hands-on development, from API design to delivery guarantees,
                concurrency and integration reliability.</p>
            <p class="contact-links">
                <a href="https://www.silverback-messaging.net" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
                    <Icon name="document"/>
                    Documentation</a>
                <a href="https://github.com/BEagle1984/silverback" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
                    <Icon name="github"/>
                    Source on GitHub</a>
            </p>
        </section>
        <section aria-labelledby="work-experience">
            <h2 id="work-experience">Work Experience</h2>
            <ol class="entries">
                <li>
                    <div class="entry-heading"><h3>Solution Architect &middot; Swiss Post</h3><span class="entry-date">2017 &ndash; present</span></div>
                    <p>Current focus: Sorting Solutions &mdash; software architecture, messaging and cloud-native systems.</p>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <div class="entry-heading"><h3>Senior .NET Developer &middot; Swiss Post</h3><span class="entry-date">2005 &ndash; 2017</span></div>
                    <p>E-commerce and postshop.ch: .NET Framework, Silverlight and team leadership.</p>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <div class="entry-heading"><h3>.NET Developer &middot; SUPSI (iCIMSI)</h3><span class="entry-date">2004 &ndash; 2005</span></div>
                    <p>International research projects and ASP.NET workflow systems.</p>
                </li>
            </ol>
        </section>
        <section aria-labelledby="education">
            <h2 id="education">Education</h2>
            <ul class="entries">
                <li><div class="entry-heading"><h3>Bachelor of Science in Computer Science</h3><span class="entry-date">2026</span></div><p>SUPSI &middot; Weighted average: 5.51/6</p></li>
                <li><div class="entry-heading"><h3>Informatics Diploma (AFC)</h3><span class="entry-date">2003</span></div><p>SPAI</p></li>
                <li><div class="entry-heading"><h3>Professional Technical Maturity</h3><span class="entry-date">2003</span></div><p>SPAI</p></li>
            </ul>
        </section>
        <section aria-labelledby="certifications">
            <h2 id="certifications">Certifications</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>SAFe&reg; 6 Architect &mdash; Scaled Agile Inc.</li>
                <li>Scrum Developer Certified &mdash; SCRUMStudy</li>
                <li>iSAQB&reg; Certified Professional for Software Architecture &mdash; Foundation Level</li>
            </ul>
        </section>
        <section aria-labelledby="skills">
            <h2 id="skills">Skills</h2>
            <dl class="skills">
                <div><dt>.NET &amp; applications</dt><dd><ul class="tags"><li>C#</li><li>.NET</li><li>Entity Framework</li><li>WPF</li><li>Angular</li><li>TypeScript</li></ul></dd></div>
                <div><dt>Architecture &amp; messaging</dt><dd><ul class="tags"><li>Microservices</li><li>Event-driven architecture</li><li>Domain-driven design</li><li>Kafka</li><li>MQTT</li></ul></dd></div>
                <div><dt>Cloud &amp; delivery</dt><dd><ul class="tags"><li>AWS</li><li>Kubernetes</li><li>Docker</li><li>Terraform</li><li>CI/CD</li><li>Git</li></ul></dd></div>
                <div><dt>Data</dt><dd><ul class="tags"><li>PostgreSQL</li><li>MongoDB</li></ul></dd></div>
                <div><dt>Engineering practices</dt><dd><ul class="tags"><li>Automated testing</li><li>Trunk-based development</li><li>Agile development</li><li>Clean code</li></ul></dd></div>
                <div><dt>Additional familiarity</dt><dd><ul class="tags"><li>Java (Spring Boot)</li><li>Python</li><li>C/C++</li></ul></dd></div>
            </dl>
        </section>
        <section aria-labelledby="outside-work">
            <h2 id="outside-work">Outside Work</h2>
            <p>Strength training, travel, scuba diving, DIY, video games, and tinkering with networks, gadgets and coding projects.</p>
        </section>

    </div>
</Layout>
